   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "adr-context-text",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 46,
   "y": 279.0,
   "width": 1488,
   "height": 160.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 967983643,
   "version": 2,
   "versionNonce": 462974932,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "• We held CTIS's list of all 12,905 trials but the full record of one: sites, MedDRA terms, translations and eligibility were not in our data.\n• 4,747 trials recruit now (CTIS status 3 or 4), by country: CTIS gives a status per member state, not per site. All are medicine trials (EU 536/2014).\n• People type short queries, condition first, often a place, in lay words and other languages, often misspelled; synonyms and “did you mean”\n  rescue most failed searches. Text alone misses: 789 recruiting trials say “cancer”, 956 more only “tumour”, “carcinoma”, “lymphoma”…\n• Exclusion criteria name diseases too (“patients with diabetes are excluded”): matching them would mislead.\n• “Paris” must be a distance, not a city's name: Gustave Roussy is in Villejuif. CTIS gives each site's city and postcode, no coordinates.\n• A public trial page needed a published judgement (ADR-007); a recruiting trial has none. Search queries are about people's health.\n• Anthropic only, every call priced; MedDRA's dictionary is licensed; MeSH (NLM) and GeoNames are free to use with credit.",
   "originalText": "• We held CTIS's list of all 12,905 trials but the full record of one: sites, MedDRA terms, translations and eligibility were not in our data.\n• 4,747 trials recruit now (CTIS status 3 or 4), by country: CTIS gives a status per member state, not per site. All are medicine trials (EU 536/2014).\n• People type short queries, condition first, often a place, in lay words and other languages, often misspelled; synonyms and “did you mean”\n  rescue most failed searches. Text alone misses: 789 recruiting trials say “cancer”, 956 more only “tumour”, “carcinoma”, “lymphoma”…\n• Exclusion criteria name diseases too (“patients with diabetes are excluded”): matching them would mislead.\n• “Paris” must be a distance, not a city's name: Gustave Roussy is in Villejuif. CTIS gives each site's city and postcode, no coordinates.\n• A public trial page needed a published judgement (ADR-007); a recruiting trial has none. Search queries are about people's health.\n• Anthropic only, every call priced; MedDRA's dictionary is licensed; MeSH (NLM) and GeoNames are free to use with credit.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "adr-context",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
